    <!-- ===== WHY VISIT CHENGDU ===== -->
    <section class="bg-surface py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="max-w-[740px]">
          <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6 reveal">Why Visit Chengdu?</h2>
          <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed reveal">
            <p>Chengdu <span class="text-[#1a1a1a] font-medium">(成都, Chéngdū)</span> has existed for over 2,200 years without changing its name, and its 21 million residents have perfected the art of slowing down. UNESCO named it a <strong class="text-[#1a1a1a]">City of Gastronomy</strong> in 2010; mapo tofu was born here in 1862, kung pao chicken in a local courtyard kitchen, and ~200 giant pandas live 30 minutes from downtown at the Chengdu Research Base.</p>
            <p>Then add the Sichuan Opera's face-changing performers, tea houses serving covered cups of jasmine tea for a millennium, and two of China's finest day trips — the 71-meter Leshan Giant Buddha and mist-shrouded Mount Qingcheng. <span class="text-[#1a1a1a] font-medium">Chengdu isn't a city you tick off a checklist — it's a city you sink into.</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

