    <section id="plan" class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-display font-semibold tracking-tight mb-2 reveal">Plan Your Trip</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-lg max-w-[52ch] mb-10 reveal">Getting around, where to stay, and when to go.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-12 reveal">
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[#1a1a1a] mb-3">Getting Around</h3>
          <div class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Metro:</span> 7+ lines, 2–7 RMB, English signs everywhere. Covers all tourist areas. The best way to get around.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Didi (滴滴):</span> China's Uber — 15–40 RMB for most trips. No language barrier — type your destination in English.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Bike sharing:</span> Hellobike and Mobike are everywhere. ¥1.50/ride. Scan QR code to unlock. Chengdu is flat and bikeable.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Taxi:</span> Plentiful, cheap, but drivers rarely speak English. Always have your destination in Chinese characters.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[#1a1a1a] mb-3">Where to Stay</h3>
          <div class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Jinli / Wuhou:</span> Tourist central. Walk to Jinli Street, Wuhou Shrine. Great for first-timers.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Kuanzhai Area:</span> Boutique hotels in converted Qing courtyards. Atmospheric, central, romantic.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Chunxi Road:</span> Shopping hub, Metro interchange, big-brand hotels. Convenient but busy.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Hi-Tech Zone:</span> Modern, quiet, spacious. Best for business travelers or families who want calm.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[#1a1a1a] mb-3">Budget Guide</h3>
          <div class="space-y-2.5 text-sm text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Backpacker:</span> ¥200–300/day — hostel, street food, Metro, one attraction.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Mid-range:</span> ¥500–800/day — boutique hotel, restaurants, Didi, all attractions.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Luxury:</span> ¥800+/day — five-star, fine dining, private driver, spa.</p>
            <p><span class="font-medium text-[#1a1a1a]">Payment:</span> WeChat Pay &amp; Alipay now accept foreign cards. Carry some cash for street stalls.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Month-by-month table -->
